WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:25.714
Type II is the bread and butter of residential HVAC. This is what you'll use
every day.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:51.429
Leak repair requirements for high-pressure comfort cooling systems: if the
annual leak rate exceeds 10 percent the owner must repair the leak within 30
days. For commercial refrigeration the trigger is 20 percent. Leak rate is

00:00:51.429 --> 00:01:17.143
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:42.857
Leak Rate: Annual refrigerant loss as a percentage of total charge. Comfort
cooling trigger is 10 percent.

00:01:42.857 --> 00:02:08.571
Here's why this matters on the job: Document all refrigerant added to a system.
This data is needed to calculate leak rates and comply with regulations.

00:02:08.571 --> 00:02:34.286
Watch out for these: 10 percent for comfort cooling. And — 20 percent for
commercial refrigeration

